-- title:
--   Elements of the different give trace functionals on S/IS
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a Noetherian integrally closed domain with fraction field $K$, and let $S$ be an integrally closed domain which is an $R$-algebra, finite and free as an $R$-module, with fraction field $F$; assume $F$ is a $K$-algebra and the various scalar actions are compatible ($R \to K \to F$ and $R \to S \to F$ are towers), and that $F$ is separable over $K$. Let $I$ be an ideal of $R$ and let $s \in S$ be an element whose image in $F$ lies in $1 / \mathrm{traceDual}_{R,K}(1)$, the $S$-submodule of elements $z \in F$ with $z \cdot \mathrm{traceDual}_{R,K}(1) \subseteq 1$, where $\mathrm{traceDual}_{R,K}(1)$ is the dual of the unit submodule $1 \subseteq F$ for the trace form of $F/K$, i.e. the set of $z \in F$ with $\mathrm{Tr}_{F/K}(z y) \in R$ for all $y$ in $1$; thus $s$ lies in the different. The conclusion is that for every $(R/I)$-linear functional $\varphi$ on $S / I S$ (with $IS$ the ideal generated by the image of $I$ under $R \to S$) there exists $x \in S/IS$ such that $\varphi(\bar s\, y) = \mathrm{Tr}_{(S/IS)/(R/I)}(x y)$ for all $y \in S/IS$.
--
--   This is the statement that the different specialises: an element of the different of a finite free extension still converts arbitrary linear functionals into trace functionals after base change along any quotient $R \to R/I$, the point being that the trace form and the dual module commute with base change for free modules. It is used by [`Algebra.mk_mem_pow_ramificationIdx_sub_one_of_mem_comap_one_div_traceDual`](thm.html#Algebra.mk_mem_pow_ramificationIdx_sub_one_of_mem_comap_one_div_traceDual), where membership in the different is converted into a statement about ramification indices on a fibre.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_Algebra_exists_forall_dual_quotient_eq_trace_of_mem_comap_one_div_traceDual.lean

import Mathlib

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false

set_option autoImplicit false

universe u

theorem Algebra.exists_forall_dual_quotient_eq_trace_of_mem_comap_one_div_traceDual
    (R : Type u) [CommRing R] [IsDomain R] [IsNoetherianRing R] [IsIntegrallyClosed R]
    (K : Type u) [Field K] [Algebra R K] [IsFractionRing R K]
    (S : Type u) [CommRing S] [IsDomain S] [IsIntegrallyClosed S] [Algebra R S] [Module.Finite R S] [Module.Free R S]
    (F : Type u) [Field F] [Algebra S F] [IsFractionRing S F] [Algebra K F] [Algebra R F]
    [IsScalarTower R K F] [IsScalarTower R S F] [Algebra.IsSeparable K F]
    (I : Ideal R) (s : S)
    (hs : s ∈ ((1 / Submodule.traceDual R K (1 : Submodule S F) : Submodule S F).comap (Algebra.linearMap S F))) :
    ∀ φ : Module.Dual (R ⧸ I) (S ⧸ I.map (algebraMap R S)),
      ∃ x : S ⧸ I.map (algebraMap R S), ∀ y : S ⧸ I.map (algebraMap R S),
        φ (Ideal.Quotient.mk (I.map (algebraMap R S)) s * y) =
          Algebra.trace (R ⧸ I) (S ⧸ I.map (algebraMap R S)) (x * y) := by sorry
